{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0049","billNumberShort":"S.B. 49","billNumberLong":"SB0049S02","fileNumber":"2026FL0074","shortTitle":"Natural Organic Reduction Amendments","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"PLUMBJ","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Plumb, Jen","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"","floorSponsorName":"","floorSponsorHouse":"","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses natural organic reduction.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>allows a funeral service establishment to offer natural organic reduction;<hr><ltbullet>requires that a funeral service director meet certain requirements if the funeral service director offers natural organic reduction;<hr><ltbullet>grants immunity to a funeral service establishment that relies on a natural organic reduction authorization form in carrying out natural organic reduction;<hr><ltbullet>updates a funeral service establishment's recordkeeping requirements;<hr><ltbullet>provides requirements for accepting remains for natural organic reduction;<hr><ltbullet>limits liability for a funeral service establishment providing natural organic reduction;<hr><ltbullet>provides the requirements for authorizing natural organic reduction;<hr><ltbullet>describes the procedure for natural organic reduction;<hr><ltbullet>provides the requirements for the final disposition of remains from the natural organic reduction process;<hr><ltbullet>categorizes the use of remains from natural organic reduction to grow food as unlawful; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Austin Weenig","fiscalAnalyst":"Noah Matthew Hansen","lastAction":"Senate/ filed","lastActionOwner":"Senate file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"ARSYIVSEVL","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionD